WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.031
An automatic dialer works without anyone watching it, so you need reports that

00:00:06.031 --> 00:00:07.348
say what it did.

00:00:07.348 --> 00:00:12.499
This video covers the Dialer activity and health report, the Dialer decision log

00:00:12.499 --> 00:00:16.511
by record and by agent, and what the states and reasons mean.

00:00:16.511 --> 00:00:22.740
It also covers the related inventory report, and the Last pacing decision on a Predictive profile.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.759
Three questions come up when a campaign seems quiet.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:32.822
Is the dialer running at all?

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:35.062
Why did it not call this record?

00:00:35.062 --> 00:00:37.420
And why did no agent get the call?

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.346
Dialer activity and health answers the first.

00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:46.016
The Dialer decision log answers the other two, by record or by agent.

00:00:46.016 --> 00:00:49.690
Both are under Reports, and need the Reports feature.

00:00:53.932 --> 00:00:57.485
Open Reports, Operations, Dialer activity and health.

00:00:57.485 --> 00:01:02.121
Dialer right now is live, and shows the State, how many paced campaigns

00:01:02.121 --> 00:01:06.999
have work waiting, and how many are stalled, idle, holding back or dialing.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:10.732
The date range only changes the counts and charts below.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.488
Campaign queues has one row for each campaign.

00:01:14.488 --> 00:01:19.209
It shows the Dialer state, when the last cycle started and completed, the

00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:22.616
Last outcome and, under Why, what the dialer found.

00:01:22.616 --> 00:01:27.397
Cycles, Calls placed, Routed to an agent and No agent available count what

00:01:27.397 --> 00:01:29.070
happened in the range.

00:01:29.529 --> 00:01:34.743
Dialer profiles shows each profile's Mode, its last cycle, and the calls it

00:01:34.743 --> 00:01:37.897
placed, answered, abandoned and suppressed.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:44.076
Below, charts show calls and campaign routing decisions over time, and Suppressed attempts

00:01:44.076 --> 00:01:47.359
by reason counts why records were not dialed.

00:01:48.959 --> 00:01:51.294
The state tells you at a glance.

00:01:51.294 --> 00:01:54.736
Dialing means calls were placed in the last cycle.

00:01:54.736 --> 00:01:58.117
Idle means work is due but no agent is available.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:03.403
Holding back means a rule, such as the abandonment policy, kept it from dialing.

00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:06.169
Nothing to call means no record is due.

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:11.716
Starting means work arrived and the first cycle has not finished.

00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:17.255
Stalled means work is due but no cycle has completed for about five minutes.

00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:22.998
Not pacing means the pacing lock was not acquired, so every cycle skips itself.

00:02:22.998 --> 00:02:26.579
Stalled and not pacing need your administrator.

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.690
Open Reports, Queue and Routing, Dialer decision log.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:41.602
The summary counts Decisions, Routing decisions, Assigned, Not assigned, Suppressions and Activities.

00:02:41.602 --> 00:02:46.189
Decisions by reason groups them, so you see the main cause first.

00:02:46.648 --> 00:02:51.480
Queues with work due now shows each queue with records waiting and due,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.056
when it last made a routing decision, and a Status.

00:02:55.056 --> 00:03:00.828
It reads Deciding, or says that no routing decision was made in the last quarter hour.

00:03:01.293 --> 00:03:03.341
Decisions lists each one.

00:03:03.341 --> 00:03:05.786
Kind is Routing or Suppression.

00:03:05.786 --> 00:03:09.353
Outcome is Assigned, Not assigned or Suppressed.

00:03:09.353 --> 00:03:14.771
Reason says why, and Candidates lists every agent that was weighed, with why

00:03:14.771 --> 00:03:17.083
each was or was not eligible.

00:03:17.537 --> 00:03:22.828
To follow one record, type its Activity ID in the filters and apply them.

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:25.641
To follow one agent, pick the agent.

00:03:25.641 --> 00:03:30.932
Campaign, Queue and Reason narrow the list, and the report shows the most

00:03:30.932 --> 00:03:34.147
recent rows, up to five hundred on screen.

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:39.246
A suppression names why a record was not dialed:

00:03:39.246 --> 00:03:43.978
No number to dial, Out of attempts, Waiting out the retry delay, Do

00:03:43.978 --> 00:03:47.607
not call, or On the national do-not-call registry.

00:03:48.357 --> 00:03:54.911
Others are Outside the calling window, Abandonment rate cap reached, Compliance check unavailable,

00:03:54.911 --> 00:03:56.927
and Number not in service.

00:03:56.927 --> 00:03:59.952
Compliance check unavailable is temporary:

00:03:59.952 --> 00:04:02.347
the record is tried again later.

00:04:03.097 --> 00:04:07.828
A routing decision that did not assign says No agents available, or No

00:04:07.828 --> 00:04:10.878
available agent matched the routing policy.

00:04:10.878 --> 00:04:13.306
The first means nobody was ready.

00:04:13.306 --> 00:04:19.157
The second means agents were ready, but skills, capacity or entitlements ruled them out.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.375
Dialer queue inventory is the live view of what is loaded.

00:04:27.375 --> 00:04:31.712
It shows each campaign's waiting, reserved and assigned records.

00:04:31.712 --> 00:04:36.110
Use it to confirm that a load arrived, and how much work is left.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:44.727
A Predictive profile that over-dials has one more place to look.

00:04:44.727 --> 00:04:50.594
On the profile's Predictive pacing card, Last pacing decision shows, for each campaign,

00:04:50.594 --> 00:04:55.705
when the last cycle ran, whether it over-dialed, reserved an agent per call

00:04:55.705 --> 00:04:57.660
or did not dial, and why.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:02.790
It also shows how many calls were placed of those allowed, the free

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:08.310
agents, the calls ringing without an agent, the answer rate and the abandonment rates.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:12.930
The table is read only, and it appears after the first over-dial cycle.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.964
A campaign went quiet:

00:05:18.964 --> 00:05:21.844
open Dialer activity and health first.

00:05:21.844 --> 00:05:27.670
The state and the Why column usually say whether it is agents, rules or the system.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.824
A contact says they were never called:

00:05:30.824 --> 00:05:34.320
find the activity in the decision log and read the reason.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.324
An agent says they got no calls:

00:05:37.324 --> 00:05:41.770
filter the decision log by that agent and read the Candidates column.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.024
Dialer activity and health tells you whether the dialer is running, and the

00:05:48.024 --> 00:05:50.755
decision log tells you why it did what it did.

00:05:50.755 --> 00:05:52.120
Thanks for watching.

